-- title:
--   The Taylor–Wiles Hecke ring is complete local and 𝒪-finite
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a noetherian local ring that is complete with respect to its maximal ideal, let $p$ be a prime with $p \in \mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$, let $N \ge 1$, $r \ge 1$ and a set $S \subseteq \mathbb N$ be given, and let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) — the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}(S_2(\Gamma_0(N)))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$, and $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$, $q \notin S$ — to the residue field of $\mathcal O$. Let $q_1,\dots,q_t$ be nonzero naturals, for each $i$ let $\pi_{\Delta,i} \colon (\mathbb Z/q_i)^\times \to \mathbb Z/p^{v_p(q_i-1)}$ (multiplicatively written) be a homomorphism, and let $\alpha_1,\dots,\alpha_t$ lie in the residue field of $\mathcal O$. Write $L = N(\prod_i q_i)r$ and $H_Q =$ `HQ N r qv p πΔ`, the intersection inside $(\mathbb Z/L)^\times$ of `HR N r qv` with the kernel of $\pi_Q = (\pi_{\Delta,i})_i$. Assume `OpComm`: the Hecke operators `op` attached to the generators indexed by `Gen L S t` commute pairwise on the carrier; assume `DiaComm`: each diamond operator [`CohCarrier.diamondL L H_Q 𝒪 u`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L55), $u \in (\mathbb Z/L)^\times$, commutes with all these Hecke operators; and assume that the localised module `ML`, namely the localisation of the carrier at the prime complement of the kernel ideal $\mathfrak m_Q$ of the map from the free polynomial algebra on the generators determined by $\theta$ and $\alpha$, is nontrivial. Then the ring `HeckeRing`, the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra `heckeSubalgebra` of endomorphisms of this localised module generated by these Hecke and diamond operators, is finite as an $\mathcal O$-module and a noetherian ring, and there is a local ring structure on it for which it is complete with respect to its maximal ideal, the structure map $\mathcal O \to$ `HeckeRing` is a local homomorphism, and the composite of this map with the residue map is surjective, i.e. `HeckeRing` has residue field that of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   This is the structure theorem for the Taylor–Wiles Hecke rings $\mathbb T_Q$ at auxiliary level $Q = \{q_1,\dots,q_t\}$: module-finiteness over $\mathcal O$, completeness, and equality of residue fields; reducedness and freeness over $\mathcal O$ are not asserted. It provides the coefficient ring over which the modular Galois representation attached to the localised cohomology module is constructed, and is used downstream to exhibit $\mathbb T_Q$ as a test object for the relevant deformation functor.
